@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components

@*
    StudentRegistrationLink — THE source of truth for the team-registration
    address, and nothing else.

    WHAT IT OWNS
    The URL. `/create-team` is the anonymous, outside-the-shell screen course
    staff share so students form teams, and deriving it in a second place is
    how two callers silently drift apart. Anything that needs this address
    renders this component rather than rebuilding the route.

    WHAT IT NO LONGER OWNS
    The copy interaction. That was thirty lines of clipboard handling, inline
    confirmation and an outline pill, and the Assignments workspace needed the
    same thirty lines for a DIFFERENT address. They now live in
    MCopyLinkAction, which this renders — same markup, same values, same
    behaviour as before, in one place instead of two.

    NOT THE ASSIGNMENT FORM. Team registration and the Project Assignment Form
    are two different student-facing screens. The old Management hub conflated
    them: it rendered this component under a tile labelled "לינק טופס שיבוצים
    לסטודנטים" while copying the registration URL. The assignment form's
    address is StudentFormLinks.AssignmentForm.

    CURRENTLY UNREFERENCED. Its only caller was that hub tile, withdrawn when
    the Management Home was curated down to destinations. The route, the page
    and this component are all intact; nothing surfaces the registration link
    today.
*@

<MCopyLinkAction Route="@Route" Label="@Label" Class="@Class" ButtonLabel="העתקת לינק" />

@code {
    /// <summary>THE address of the team-registration screen. A route, not a
    /// URL — MCopyLinkAction resolves it against the app's own base URI, so no
    /// environment hostname is written down anywhere.</summary>
    public const string Route = "create-team";

    /// <summary>What the link is called where it is shown. Defaulted rather
    /// than required, so the common case is a bare
    /// &lt;StudentRegistrationLink /&gt;.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "לינק הרשמת צוותים לסטודנטים";

    /// <summary>Positioning only — the caller owns where this sits.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
